course: dictionary
lesson: 676
title: Place names and the words that come from them
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Balkan is one of them. It describes things to do with the Balkans, a mountainous region in south-east Europe. The capital B is a clue: Balkan names a place, so it starts with a capital letter.
explain: The Balkans is a noun for the region itself. When Balkan comes before another word, like Balkan mountains or Balkan music, it tells you the thing belongs to that region.
explain: Read the words around it to work out where a place is. «Then up the Adriatic (the sea between Italy and the Balkans) and into Venice down a path of gold, as the sun rose behind them.» The bracket tells you the Adriatic lies between Italy and the Balkans, so the Balkans are on the other side of that sea from Italy.
fact: Balkan is an adjective when it describes something, such as Balkan food or Balkan mountains.
fact: The Balkans is a noun for the region, a mountainous area in south-east Europe.
fact: The Balkans includes countries such as Greece, Albania, Bulgaria, Serbia and Croatia.
fact: The Balkan Mountains are in Bulgaria.
fact: Balkan and Balkans start with a capital letter because they are names of a place.
exercise: Where is the Adriatic, according to «up the Adriatic» (the sea between Italy and the Balkans)? | Inside the Balkan Mountains | *Between Italy and the Balkans | Far away in the Pacific Ocean
exercise: Which of these is a country in the Balkans? | Japan | *Bulgaria | Brazil
exercise: «The Balkan Mountains are in Bulgaria.» What does Balkan tell you about the mountains? | They are made of sand | *They belong to the Balkan region, in south-east Europe | They are the tallest mountains in Africa
test: Balkan is used before a word like «Balkan music». What kind of word is it there? | A verb, which shows action | A noun, which names a thing | *An adjective, which describes a noun
test: Which word in «up the Adriatic (the sea between Italy and the Balkans)» names a sea? | *Adriatic | Venice | Balkans
exam: What is the Balkans? | An island in the Pacific | *A mountainous region in south-east Europe | A city in Italy
